<article class="env-lemma" id="0BLG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BLG">Lemma <span data-tag="0BLG">58.19.2</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0BLF" data-tag="0BLF">58.19.1</a>. Assume one of the following holds </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\dim (A/\mathfrak p) \geq 2$ for every minimal prime $\mathfrak p \subset A$ with $f \not\in \mathfrak p$, or 
</p>
</li><li><p>
every connected component of $U$ meets $U_0$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \textit{FÉt}_ U \longrightarrow \textit{FÉt}_{U_0},\quad V \longmapsto V_0 = V \times _ U U_0  \]
</div>
  <p> is a faithful functor. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Case (2) is immediate from Lemma <a href="/tag/0EJX" data-tag="0EJX">58.17.5</a>. Assumption (1) implies every irreducible component of $U$ meets $U_0$, see Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00KW" data-tag="00KW">10.60.13</a>. Hence (1) follows from (2). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>